", "Sexual activity without barrier protection", "Ordered urinary β-hCG test (suggesting reproductive aetiology consideration)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Acute cholecystitis: rapid weight loss and RUQ pain suggest gallbladder pathology", "Ectopic pregnancy: sexually active, β-hCG ordered, but lacks classic pregnancy symptoms", "Alcoholic pancreatitis: chronic alcohol use, but pain pattern is more epigastric/upper abdominal", "Ovarian torsion or ruptured cyst: shock and RUQ pain could overlap, but less likely with diffuse tenderness"], "alarm_features": ["Shock or major haemodynamic instability (hypotension and tachycardia)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Source", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.38216560509554137, "posterior": 0.40144378175672857, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Hypotension and tachycardia could indicate hypovolemic shock from a ruptured ectopic pregnancy. The pending β-hCG test and lack of barrier protection support t…"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of classic pregnancy symptoms and gynecologic findings (pelvic tenderness, masses) reduces the likelihood of a pelvic source, supporting considerat…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Pathology", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.45859872611464975, "posterior": 0.1381725489215498, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The absence of classic pregnancy symptoms and gynecologic findings (pelvic tenderness, masses) reduces the likelihood of a pelvic source, supporting considerat…"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of jaundice, ascites, and hepatomegaly on exam argues against Budd-Chiari syndrome, which typically presents with these findings."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Obstruction", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.044, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The lack of Charcot triad signs (fever, jaundice) and hemodynamic instability significantly reduces the likelihood of biliary obstruction as the cause."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Pancreatic Pathology", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.029, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Localized RUQ pain without epigastric/back radiation is inconsistent with pancreatic pathology, which typically presents with epigastric pain radiating to the …"]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Ectopic Pregnancy with Hemorrhagic Shock", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.011, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Classic pregnancy symptoms are absent, which weakens ectopic pregnancy's likelihood, but β-hCG testing remains critical for confirmation."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Ruptured Hemorrhagic Ovarian Cyst", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.041, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Localized RUQ pain without pelvic findings weakly argues against ovarian cyst rupture as the primary source."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Ovarian Torsion with Ischemia", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.35, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Bud